{"book":{"id":"book-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat","slug":"scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat","title":"Scars on the Land: An Environmental History of Slavery in the American South","authors":[{"id":"person-david-silkenat","name":"David Silkenat"}],"isbn13":["9780197564257"],"subjects":["American History"],"topics":["Slavery & Emancipation","Black History & Culture","Environment, Conservation & Pollution","Food, Agriculture & Land"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Scars%20on%20the%20Land%3A%20An%20Environmental%20History%20of%20Slavery%20in%20the%20American%20South%20David%20Silkenat","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Scars%20on%20the%20Land%3A%20An%20Environmental%20History%20of%20Slavery%20in%20the%20American%20South%20David%20Silkenat","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Scars%20on%20the%20Land%3A%20An%20Environmental%20History%20of%20Slavery%20in%20the%20American%20South%20David%20Silkenat","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Scars%20on%20the%20Land%3A%20An%20Environmental%20History%20of%20Slavery%20in%20the%20American%20South%20David%20Silkenat","publisher":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Scars_on_the_Land.html?hl=&id=mjFnzwEACAAJ"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-frederick-douglass-slavery-abolition-gilder-lehrman-center-official-2023-finalist-announcement","source-google-books-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat","source-open-library-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat","source-cover-open-library-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat"],"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Plantation workers","sourceId":"source-google-books-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat"}],"publicationYear":2022,"summary":"They worked Virginia's tobacco fields, South Carolina's rice marshes, and the Black Belt's cotton plantations. Wherever they lived, enslaved people found their lives indelibly shaped by the Southern environment. By day, they plucked worms and insects from the crops, trod barefoot in the mud as they hoed rice fields, and endured the sun and humidity as they planted and harvested the fields. By night, they clandestinely took to the woods and swamps to trap opossums and turtles, to visit relatives living on adjacent plantations, and at times to escape slave patrols and escape to freedom. This book presents a comprehensive history of American slavery to examine how the environment fundamentally formed enslaved people's lives and how slavery remade the Southern landscape.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-scars-on-the-land-an-environmental-history-of-slavery-in-the-american-south-david-silkenat.jpg","displaySummary":"This book presents a comprehensive history of American slavery to examine how the environment fundamentally formed enslaved people's lives and how slavery remade the Southern landscape.","primarySubject":"American History","primaryTopic":"Slavery & Emancipation","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"American History","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"American History","score":4,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Nature & Environment","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Travel & Place","score":2,"evidenceCount":1},{"subject":"Business & Economics","score":1,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"American History","mappedSubject":"American History","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"American history keyword; history keyword or history prize; nature/environment keyword; race/ethnicity keyword; travel/place keyword","id":"su